<newsitem itemid="50054" id="root" date="1996-09-12" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: William Baird H1 pre-tax profits slip.</title>
<headline>William Baird H1 pre-tax profits slip.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year to June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence) pre-excep  4.4		    vs 4.9</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		2.0		    vs 4.9</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 3.55		   vs 3.55</p>
<p> Pretax pre-excep	 7.9		    vs 8.4</p>
<p> Pretax		     5.1		    vs 8.4</p>
<p> Turnover		   303.6		  vs 304.0</p>
<p> Operating profit	 10.68		  vs 10.72</p>
<p> Exceptional charge     2.80		   vs nil</p>
<p> Interest		   2.76		   vs 2.32</p>
<p> Tax			  2.83		   vs 2.78</p>
<p> Net taxed		  2.30		   vs 5.63</p>
<p> Pay date		   Jan 1, 1997</p>
<p>Div registration date  Dec 12, 1996</p>
<p>NOTE--Clothing maker and designer William Baird's chairman Donald Parr said retail sales growth in the UK is showing signs of modest improvement but strong resistance remains against price increases. &quot;However, the trading pattern to date suggests that more normal trading conditions are likely to prevail in the second half compared to the exceptionally difficult conditions experienced in the same period last year.&quot;</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
